{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1111927-2e-seeking-feedback-on-a-merit-i-m-suggesting-to-my-storyteller","id":1111927,"title":"[2E] Seeking Feedback on a Merit I'm Suggesting to My Storyteller","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-05T18:35:32-07:00","id":1111927,"title":"[2E] Seeking Feedback on a Merit I'm Suggesting to My Storyteller","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I'm very new to Mage: the Awakening 2E (creating my first character, in fact), and I'm already contemplating submitting a custom Merit to my Storyteller. He suggested I post here for some feedback first, so here I am! Thanks in advance for any insights you can provide.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Problem</b></span><br /> I was disappointed by the way the mechanics seem to favor generic, all-purpose Yantras (e.g. +2 from High Speech/Runes) over those that encourage creativity or imaginative descriptions of &quot;how&quot; a spell is cast (e.g. only +1 from personalized magical tools, or for coming up with an interesting place/time Yantra). With most starting characters limited to one or two Yantras per spell, it seems to me there's pressure to gravitate towards the same boring High Speech, generic Runes, or other &quot;one-size-fits-all&quot; +2 effects whenever possible. Yes, I'm well aware that there are many times a mage won't be able to loudly chant in High Speech for three hours, or inscribe runes, or otherwise take advantage of these generic +2 Yantras... but I still dislike the idea that, all things being equal, a player who designs a clever and creative ritual is going to roll fewer dice than a player who simply falls back on High Speech.<br /> <br /> That being said, I emphasize I'm very new to Mage 2E, and it's quite possible that I (and my Storyteller) missed something in the rules that makes moot the above concerns. If so, uh, then the rest of this post may well have been a waste of time and energy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Proposal</b></span><br /> A new Merit, similar in function to Shadow Name, that rewards investing imagination/effort/time/complexity/creativity to create a &quot;custom Yantra&quot; (one tailored to a specific spell) with a die bonus worthy of the effort:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">INVENTIVE (2-3 dots)</span></b></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Effect:</b> Perhaps due to curiosity, daring, wanderlust or rebellion, you were driven to explore the lesser-travelled twists and turns of your Path, to stray from the reliable, conventional methods of the Art in search of different inspiration. Among the infinite expanse of magical techniques, you found that inspiration <i>everywhere</i>: a bottomless toolbox of magical techniques, from which you have learned to design &quot;custom Yantras&quot; that are uniquely-tailored to specific spells. The intimate link between a custom Yantra and its spell affords you an especially-powerful aid to forming Imago.<br /> <br /> A custom Yantra must be bound to a specific spell, which you define in advance following the guidelines for creating a Rote, and can be either <i>reusable</i> or <i>consumable</i>:</div><ul><li>A reusable custom Yantra can be used whenever you cast its associated spell, for a dice bonus equal to this Merit's dots.</li> <li>A consumable custom Yantra is destroyed (or otherwise spent) when you cast its spell, for a dice bonus equal to this Merit's dots <i>plus one</i>.</li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Creating a custom Yantra takes time and effort:</div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Define the spell to which the custom Yantra will apply, as if creating a Rote. Specify whether it will be reusable or consumable.</li> <li>Work with your Storyteller to design the custom Yantra itself. This may impose further narrative requirements, which you must satisfy before completing your work (e.g. accessing a location, acquiring materials, gaining information).</li> <li>Make an extended roll, with Traits and a time interval set by the Storyteller (determined by the nature of the work you're doing to actually create the custom Yantra):</li> </ol><ul><li>For a <i>reusable</i> custom Yantra, the time interval cannot be shorter than the Ritual Interval specified by your Gnosis. Target successes equal this Merit's dots multiplied by the <i>highest</i> Arcanum used in the spell.</li> <li>For a <i>consumable</i> custom Yantra, the time interval is not limited by Gnosis. Target successes equal this Merit's dots multiplied by the <i>lowest</i> Arcanum used in the spell.</li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Your custom Yantra bears no resemblance to the associated spell's Imago: it isn't a Yantra at all. All expendable resources used in its construction are lost.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>You create a flawed, but still functional, custom Yantra. Decrease its dice bonus by one, and it won't be winning any beauty contests.<br /> <b>Success: </b> You complete your custom Yantra more-or-less as designed.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b> You craft a custom Yantra that is especially well-suited to the Imago of its associated spell. Increase its dice bonus by one, and the elegance of its design is obvious to all.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>E.g. A Libertine with Gnosis 2 wants to program a mobile app that he can use to scan for life in his vicinity (i.e. Life 1, &quot;Web of Life&quot;). After satisfying the Storyteller with a description of the planned custom Yantra (&quot;a radar screen that reveals the spell's findings as color-coded dots&quot;), the Storyteller asks him to make an extended programming roll: Intelligence + Computers, with a time interval of 3 hours (the minimum allowed by his Gnosis Ritual Interval), and a target of 3 successes (the Libertine has 3 dots in this Merit, and this is a Life 1 spell). If successful, the Libertine will have programmed a mobile app that he can use as a +3 Yantra when casting Web of Life.</i></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Drawback:</b> A custom Yantra cannot be used alongside a Dedicated Magical Tool to reduce Paradox dice. Moreover, spells cast using a custom Yantra leave a distinctive residue, providing a +2 bonus to Revelation rolls made to read your Signature Nimbus.</div>Thoughts? Feedback? Overripe vegetables hurled in vituperative rage? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />4","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":13110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","user":"Eunomiac","date":". 07-05-2017, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T20:51:27-07:00","id":1111968,"title":"","content":"Firstly, magic is SUPPOSED to be hard for new mages (and oftentimes still is for veterans). It's literally in the design of the game.<br /> <br /> Secondly, my understanding of the game is that yantras that give more than a +1 dice bonus aren't supposed to be easy to acquire. This is why new mages are taught High Speech and the use of magic tools: they're easy to acquire and use. Sure, you can find your place of power that gives a +2 environmental yantra bonus to some spells, and you have your mighty mudra yantras used in rotes, and don't forget about that juicy Shadow Name persona yantra. However, by design yantras that give more than a +1 bonus tend to be limited in some form or fashion (whereas +1 yantras are limited in power).<br /> <br /> Thirdly, this kind of gameline is one where the onus is on you to roleplay out the flavor and fluff you want. Yantras that can be semiotically linked to a spell can be as flavorful as you want them to be, but that doesn't necessitate an increase in it's mechanical power. That just means you're doing your job as a player to make the game and your character more interesting.<br /> <br /> Fourthly, don't forget that you can add 3 dice to your spellcasting pool from willpower point expenditure that doesn't count towards yantra limits.<br /> <br /> Fifthly, because I don't think this can be understated (and because it is critical to the game's setting), I'm going to say it again: Magic is SUPPOSED to be hard for new mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> All that being said, investing experience into a merit does qualify you for potentially receiving a yantra that provides a bonus higher than a single dice.<br /> However, I believe that it's poor design to make a merit that can create any category of yantra you want. Remember, even with the xp expenditure, such yantras are still limited. Rather, it's probably better to make a merit that's specific to your character.<br /> <br /> Final note, the mechanic of requiring a number of successes to succeed at a task is mostly done away with in second edition. Extended tasks can still have them, but frankly speaking you're almost exclusively going to be casting as an instant action. Ritual casting is NOT the norm for players. Npc mages? Maybe. Players? No. <br /> <br /> Hope this info helps. \ud83d\ude01<br /> <br /> P.s. I do have to say that I like you're creativity. It's exactly the right attitude to take. Personally, I think that Shadow Name probably has a lot of room to cover your roleplaying needs, but I love that you want to try to get people more involved in the roleplay aspect. If I were the ST, I would find some way to work with you on this.<br /> <br /> P.p.s, I'm tired and didn't read you're post fully. I apologize for that and will get you more feedback tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 07-06-2017, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T22:19:47-07:00","id":1111980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eunomiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1111927-2e-seeking-feedback-on-a-merit-i-m-suggesting-to-my-storyteller#post1111927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With most starting characters limited to one or two Yantras per spell, it seems to me there's pressure to gravitate towards the same boring High Speech, generic Runes, or other &quot;one-size-fits-all&quot; +2 effects whenever possible. Yes, I'm well aware that there are many times a mage won't be able to loudly chant in High Speech for three hours, or inscribe runes, or otherwise take advantage of these generic +2 Yantras... but I still dislike the idea that, all things being equal, a player who designs a clever and creative ritual is going to roll fewer dice than a player who simply falls back on High Speech.</div> </div> </div> </div>All things being equal, a player who simply falls back on High Speech is outright risking Quiescence and not using many of their Yantra slots unless they're hanging out at the lowest levels of Gnosis, at which point they need to spend three hours drawing to use Runes in the first place. The most potent Yantras a mage has access to off-the-cuff either correspond to specific spells or reflect their spells as Things They Can Just Do with a well-kept magical identity; the benefits of ESS Yantras lie in the breadth of symbolic options they reflect, and the benefits of tools are primarily versatility and Dedication.<br /> <br /> Starting characters gravitating toward more broad-scope Yantras if given no reason not to is kind of within spec for Mage \u2014 potentially exposing Sleepers to High Speech tends to be off the list of Best Practices and the sanctity of ritual spaces is not something to be relied upon out in the field with spells you don't know a mudra for, so you lean on your specialties as often as possible while you fill in the gaps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thoughts? Feedback? Overripe vegetables hurled in vituperative rage? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>This feels like it would be better served as a Merit that lets you gain a benefit akin to those for exceptional success on castings made using a given type of Instrument; dismissing the default benefit as &quot;only&quot; a +1 and then making a Merit that effectively lets you make +2-+4 versions of +1 Yantras doesn't really help make the case against &quot;generic&quot; and &quot;boring&quot; Action bonuses.<br /> <br /> Some alternative suggestions, thrown together off-the-cuff:<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: Efficient Consumption (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character has streamlined her magic to better utilize a common practice. When using a Sacrament Yantra that is also a Sympathy Yantra, the combined bonus is treated as a single Yantra.<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: A Sense for Time and Place (\u2022\u2022)<br /> Effect:</b> Your character has a knack for drawing out the potential of times and places in the Fallen World in her spellcasting. When using a Place Yantra (whether it be a Supernal Verge or a more conventional Environment), you may take one of the benefits of exceptional success on any successful spellcasting roll, chosen by the Storyteller based on the spell and the symbolism of the Yantra. (You do not gain Willpower from the use of this Merit, but the benefit does apply in addition to any gained on a rolled exceptional success.)<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Gaining the benefits of this Merit in a Demesne or Supernal Verge requires forfeiting the normal Paradox-mitigating effect of those locations on the spell.<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: Path of [Instrument]s (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character has gained an affinity for a particular segment of Awakened symbolism, and it shapes her magical practice. When purchasing this Merit, choose a type of Path tool. Spellcasting rolls gain the 9-Again benefit if they use that tool as a Yantra, or the 8-Again benefit if their highest Arcanum is one of your Ruling Arcana. Using that type of tool as a Dedicated Instrument negates the cumulative Paradox dice from successive Paradox rolls for spells that benefit from its symbolism.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Spells from your Path's Inferior Arcanum do not benefit from the 10-Again rule unless they meet the symbolism of your chosen Path tool. Paradox dice from successive Paradox rolls still accumulate and are applied to any Paradox rolls made for spells that do not benefit from the Path tool's symbolism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T01:20:55-07:00","id":1112008,"title":"","content":"Shadow Name is basically the Yantra where as long as you're acting in character you can use whatever props you want to cast spells that fit the role defined by your Shadow Name. In the end it's all about the Shadow Name's bonus, but it can -look- like whatever you want.<br /> <br /> Also, you should feel free to ask your ST if there happens to be an appropriate prop lying around that can be used as a Yantra (Especially if you have Prime sight) which will let you riff off your ST's setting. Collect, claim and carry or remember those things as part of your journey to building up the eclectic repertoire of a Master.<br /> <br /> I'm not sold on the Merit you're suggesting, but that's mostly because I don't consider myself a good judge of them until after I've after I've tested it out. It does seem like a really limited application of Shadow Name to me though, it could be a way to invest in magic that lets you &quot;break&quot; character, but if so I'd add a drawback. Something like the magic more easily leaks out to your Sympathetic connections using the Yantra as a vector perhaps. (I.e. Your mom starts getting weird push notifications from your Web of Life app or something)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}